  "question": {
    "text": "In the following reaction sequence, the major product $\\mathbf{P}$ is formed.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/65VJZ6IJy8c-o86buKSkQTtePbf-UUSpW1Eyd2PytE8.original.fullsize.png\">\nGlycerol reacts completely with excess $\\mathbf{P}$ in the presence of an acid catalyst to form $\\mathbf{Q}$. Reaction of $\\mathbf{Q}$ with excess $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ followed by the treatment with $\\mathrm{CaCl}_2$ yields Ca-soap $\\mathbf{R}$, quantitatively. Starting with one mole of $\\mathbf{Q}$, the amount of $\\mathbf{R}$ produced in gram is ________.\n[Given, atomic weight: $\\mathrm{H}=1, \\mathrm{C}=12, \\mathrm{~N}=14, \\mathrm{O}=16, \\mathrm{Na}=23, \\mathrm{Cl}=35, \\mathrm{Ca}=40$ ]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": 909,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/FU-LArOFMNrHyc3DDcQnVLpDwqlq5F_MME0WmISMut0.original.fullsize.png\">\n$\\frac{3}{2}$ mole soap. $=\\frac{3}{2} \\times 606 \\mathrm{gm}=909 \\mathrm{gm}$",
